Z||000005||Standard||07-19-2000||03:18 AM||||One of the guys I work with drives a '96 Police Intercepter, a Ford Crown Vic set-up for the highway chases.  Still has the cage in it.. <P>Not too fast off the line, but above 50 it flat out <I>hauls</I>..  I took a peek at the front suspension and there is one <B>beefy</B> swaybar there, and the suspension to match.  For such a big car, it handles unbelievably good.  I don't think it could keep up with a modded Fiero, tho.  <P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 147,000 miles and counting!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||My7Fieros||07-19-2000||03:47 AM||||Yeah we treat our squad cars like s*&t! Ever see a 99 Crown Vic w/a cajillion miles on it? lol....man Im tired...nite all! lol||||reg||1
Z||000007||Boodoggin||07-19-2000||11:29 AM||||cool does this mean Im finally going to see a fiero on worlds wildest police chases.  <P><BR>Where Im from some police still drive mustang 5.0 police interceptors.  They sell them to the public when thier done.  Ive always wanted one.<p>[This message has been edited by Boodoggin (edited 07-19-2000).]||||reg||1
